      "writtenOn": "2024-09-24T21:11:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I know this was requested by the external reporter, but I\u0027m not convinced this is what we want.\n\nIf it\u0027s in the default orientation, encoding it in EXIF stores extra unnecessary information - how many bytes does this use?\n\nOptionally storing it seems reasonable, though? Maybe they\u0027re using a higher level API that doesn\u0027t get to modify `SkJpegEncoder::Options`?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 7,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "da24ad6235479471c85e447124a1cb684d7c635c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f1c8becb_de9a6001",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 7,
      "author": {
        "id": 3568682
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-25T13:06:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently there is no default orientation in the encoded image and `SkJpegEncoder::Options` doesn\u0027t have an `origin` field, the user wants the data to exist so that they can modify it while encoded. The current implementation is that the orientation is read as default when the data doesn\u0027t exist at decode.",
      "parentUuid": "ae252f80_27147d41",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 7,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 7,
        "endChar": 6
      },
      "revId": "da24ad6235479471c85e447124a1cb684d7c635c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
